uarter view of an older white man who is smiling and pointing to the camera. He is holding a toddler who is dressed in a winter jacket and white stocking hat. The man is also wearing a jacket and a navy blue t-shirt with a bright green Prevent Cancer Foundation imprint.】 【47†Image: A three-quarter view of an older white man who is smiling and pointing to the camera. He is holding a toddler who is dressed in a winter jacket and white stocking hat.\nL61: The man is also wearing a jacket and a navy blue t-shirt with a bright green Prevent Cancer Foundation imprint.】\nL62: ALL ABOUT THE\nL63: # Prevent Cancer Foundation\nL64: \nL65: Taking the power from cancer and giving it to the people\nL66: \nL67: The Prevent Cancer Foundation^{®} is the only U.S.-based nonprofit organization solely dedicated to cancer prevention and early detection. Our vision is a world where cancer is preventable, detectable and beatable for all.\nL68: ## Foundation Details\nL69: \nL70: Get in the weeds on the Foundation’s rich history, culture and stewardship.\nL71: \nL72: 【48†Donate】\nL73: \nL74: 【49†Image: A list of four charity seals from Guidestar, Better Business Bureau, Charity Navigator and Charity Watch.】 【49†Image: A list of four charity seals from Guidestar, Better Business Bureau, Charity Navigator and Charity Watch.】\nL75:   * 【50†Foundation History】\nL76:   * 【51†Financials】\nL77:   * 【52†Team】\nL78:   * 【53†Board of Directors】\nL79:   * 【54†Medical Advisory Board】\nL80:   * 【55†Health Equity】\nL81:   * 【56†Latest News】\nL82:   * 【57†Careers】\nL83: \nL84: \nL85: \nL86: The Foundation was founded in 1985 and carries out its work in four areas:\nL87: Research: The Foundation funds research grants and fellowships at some of the most prestigious academic institutions and medical centers across the U.S. The goal of the Foundation’s research program is to identify and fund innovative projects with the potential to make substantial contributions to cancer prevention and early detection.\nL88: Education: The Foundation is committed to providing evidence-based information about how to prevent cancer or detect it early through healthy lifestyle choices, vaccinations and medical screenings.\nL89: \nL90: Advocacy: By engaging policymakers and grassroots supporters through advocacy, the Foundation promotes increased funding for research and supports legislation that reduces disparities and improves access to care and screenings.\nL91: Community: The Foundation works closely with community-based organizations through our Community Exchange network and supports programs and grants to act locally. By empowering those who know their communities best, the Foundation is able to implement lifesaving programs that benefit all populations, especially the medically underserved.\nL92: ### Our mission is: Stopping Cancer. Saving Lives.\nL93: \nL94: ## Bold goals for reducing cancer deaths by 40%\nL95: \nL96: Rising to meet the challenge by 2035\nL97: \nL98: 【58†Image: Dr. Craig Jordan, wearing a lab coat and posing in his research lab】 【58†Image: Dr. Craig Jordan, wearing a lab coat and posing in his research lab】\nL99: #### $20 million for research\nL100: \nL101: Funding research in innovative technologies to detect cancer early and advance multi-cancer screening\nL102: \nL103: 【59†Image: Dr. Kathleen Schmeler holding a medical instrument and surrounded by a group of local nurses and doctors in Mozambique, Brazil】 【59†Image: Dr. Kathleen Schmeler holding a medical instrument and surrounded by a group of local nurses and doctors in Mozambique, Brazil】\nL104: #### $10 million for access\nL105: \nL106: Expanding cancer screening and vaccination access to medically underserved communities\nL107: \nL108: 【60†Image: A Fondation staff person is behind a behind a table at a health fair wearing a bright green shirt. She is handing out materials to a group of people.】 【60†Image: A Fondation staff person is behind a behind a table at a health fair wearing a bright green shirt. She is handing out materials to a group of people.】\nL109: #### $10 million for education\nL110: \nL111: Informing the public about screening and vaccination options so they can stay ahead of cancer\nL112: ### Prevention news for you\nL113: \nL114: \"*\" indicates required fields\nL115: \nL116: [Input]\nL117: \nL118: Email*\nL119: \nL120: [Input: Email Address]\nL121: \nL122: [Button: Submit] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL123: \nL124: This site is protected by reCAPTCHA and the Google 【61†Privacy Policy†policies.google.com】 and 【62†Terms of Service†policies.google.com】 apply.\nL125: \nL126:   * Contact:\nL127:   * pcf@preventcancer.org\nL128:   * (703) 836-4412\nL129: 333 John Carlyle Street, Suite 635\nL130: Alexandria, VA 22314\nL131: The Prevent Cancer Foundation’s mission is: Stopping Cancer. Saving Lives.\nL132: \nL133: 【63†Image: an illustration of a double helix that is part of the Prevent Cancer Foundation logo. This version is striped and includes the inclusive colors of the pride flag.】Whenever possible, the Foundation uses inclusive language and avoids unnecessary expressions of sex or gender. Some copy uses language dictated by the scientific research it is based upon.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOverview of Prevent Cancer Foundation outreach program (https://preventcancer.org/education-outreach/)\nciteturn2view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://preventcancer.org/education-outreach/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 178\nL0: 【0†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Prevent Cancer Foundation】\nL3: \nL4:   * 【2†Skip to navigation Accesskey \"n\"】\nL5:   * 【3†Skip to content Accesskey \"c\"】\nL6:   * 【4†Skip to footer Accesskey \"f\"】\nL7: \nL8: 【5†Search】\nL9: \nL10: 【6†Menu】\nL11: \nL12: 【7†Donate】\nL13:   * 【8†Prevention & Screening】 [2]\nL14:     * 【9†Ways t